WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.125
Open the Office toolbox page and choose Uninstall only.

00:00:04.125 --> 00:00:07.042
This is separate from installation.

00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:11.917
First confirm that you intend to remove the existing Office installation.

00:00:11.917 --> 00:00:16.333
Save every open document and back up settings you need to keep.

00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:24.458
The removal described on the page removes Office and clears its related configuration, licensing, services and
caches.

00:00:24.458 --> 00:00:29.583
Choose PowerShell or CMD to match the actual administrator terminal.

00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:34.042
Read the removal notice carefully before moving on to copying.

00:00:34.042 --> 00:00:37.875
Click Copy full command or download its text.

00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:45.042
Do not run it on a computer whose purpose you are unsure of, and do not confuse this command with the
installation command.

00:00:45.042 --> 00:00:48.750
After pasting, check the removal scope again.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:52.958
This is only an illustration: no uninstall is run.

00:00:52.958 --> 00:00:58.667
Before pressing Enter, confirm that your documents are saved and your settings backed up.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:03.000
If uninstalling reports an error, keep the message and stop.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.750
The script does not continue deep cleanup after an uninstall failure.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:11.583
A started command is not a completed uninstall.

00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:14.167
Check the actual output.
